**2. Filling the table for substrings of length `len` from 2 to `n`:**
For each `len`:
  For `i` from 0 to `n - len`:
    `j = i + len - 1`
    For `k` from `i` to `j - 1`: (split point)
      `P[i][j]` = `P[i][j]` U {A | A -> BC, B in `P[i][k]`, C in `P[k+1][j]`}

**Length 2 (len=2):** `P[i][i+1]`
*   `P[0][1]` (`t32 t2`): `P[0][0]`={NT30}, `P[1][1]`={NT13}. No rule `X -> NT30 NT13`. -> {}
*   `P[1][2]` (`t2 t3`): `P[1][1]`={NT13}, `P[2][2]`={NT22}. Rule `S -> NT13 NT22`. -> {S}
*   `P[2][3]` (`t3 t32`): `P[2][2]`={NT22}, `P[3][3]`={NT30}. No rule `X -> NT22 NT30`. -> {}
