*   `P[4][5]` (`t2 t18`): `P[4][4]`={NT13}, `P[5][5]`={NT6}. No rule `X -> NT13 NT6`. -> {}
*   `P[5][6]` (`t18 t41`): `P[5][5]`={NT6}, `P[6][6]`={NT32}. No rule `X -> NT6 NT32`. -> {}
*   `P[6][7]` (`t41 t16`): `P[6][6]`={NT32}, `P[7][7]`={NT30}. No rule `X -> NT32 NT30`. -> {}
*   `P[7][8]` (`t16 t8`): `P[7][7]`={NT30}, `P[8][8]`={NT6}. No rule `X -> NT30 NT6`. -> {}
*   `P[8][9]` (`t8 t6`): `P[8][8]`={NT6}, `P[9][9]`={NT6}. No rule `X -> NT6 NT6`. -> {}
*   `P[9][10]` (`t6 t6`): `P[9][9]`={NT6}, `P[10][10]`={NT6}. No rule `X -> NT6 NT6`. -> {}
*   `P[10][11]` (`t6 t30`): `P[10][10]`={NT6}, `P[11][11]`={NT22}. No rule `X -> NT6 NT22`. -> {}
*   `P[11][12]` (`t30 t20`): `P[11][11]`={NT22}, `P[12][12]`={NT32}. No rule `X -> NT22 NT32`. -> {}
*   `P[12][13]` (`t20 t3`): `P[12][12]`={NT32}, `P[13][13]`={NT22}. No rule `X -> NT32 NT22`. -> {}
*   `P[13][14]` (`t3 t16`): `P[13][13]`={NT22}, `P[14][14]`={NT30}. No rule `X -> NT22 NT30`. -> {}

At this stage, the only cell `P[i][j]` with `i != j` that contains any non-terminal is `P[1][2]` = {S}. All other cells representing substrings of length 2 are empty.

**3. Continuing for longer substrings:**
For any `P[i][j]` (where `j-i+1 > 2`) to be non-empty, it must be formed by combining two non-empty sets `P[i][k]` and `P[k+1][j]`.

Let's trace:
*   `P[0][2]` (`t32 t2 t3`):
    *   `k=0`: `P[0][0]`={NT30}, `P[1][2]`={S}. No rule `X -> NT30 S`.
